I call it "pipeline" as shorthand for pipeline system. 

I may stand corrected by someone with better information, but I believe the system consist of 3 major pipelines at 56-, 48- and 30-to-26-inches in diameter. The two major lines are fully dedicated to crude, and the 3rd smaller can carry crude and/or NGLs. My understanding is that several sections of the pipeline had been reinforced with additional parallel piping (some sections run in 6 different lines). The system has 11 pumping stations running at total of ~65 turbines for power generation, which in turn move pumping units).

@TankerTrackers All good. Appreciate if someone has confirmation of the number of main conduits on the system. I believe it is 3.

